% review-findings: Last verse: a mock wedding ("Now you married I give you joy, first a gal an' second a boy") ending "give her a kiss an' send her out". Mild, and common in playground versions.
% review-suggestion: Keep the full text in the file as the source, and end the class version before "Now you married" (the ring game works without it).
% review-decision: published to main on 11 November 2026 without the last verse (bars 25-32, the mock wedding that ends with a kiss), as the review suggested; the full text stays here as the source; keep correcting here
