O:Jamaica
R:ring game
S:Walter Jekyll (ed.), Jamaican Song and Story (London: David Nutt, 1907), Project Gutenberg #35410 (music as MusicXML), no. LXXXIX, p. 191
N:Words and tune as Jekyll printed them: Andante, then Allegro where the pair wheel. The boys and girls join hands and form a ring; one crouches in the middle as Sally Water, rises slowly at "Rise, Sally, rise", brushing away imaginary tears, turns one way and another, and chooses a partner from the ring.
